{
  "dom_id": "step-e132",
  "name": "Example: Determining Which Functions are Differentiable at a Given Point From the Function Expressions",
  "problem": "Which of the following functions are differentiable at the point $x=-1?$\n\n- $f(x) = x^5+1$\n\n- $g(x) = \\dfrac{2}{x+1}$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each function individually.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is a polynomial and is therefore differentiable and continuous for all $x.$\n\n- The function $g(x)$ has an essential discontinuity at $x=-1,$ so it is not differentiable at $x=-1$ either.\n\nIn conclusion, only $f(x)$ is differentiable at the point $x=-1.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
